# Note: the master *.png photos ARE tracked on purpose. They are the
# originals that build.py --images reworks into site/images/. They are
# never served to visitors because only site/ is deployed.

# Safety net. Caledon Storefront.png is a photograph of ANOTHER COMPANY's
# premises - their sign is on the building. It shipped with the shared photo
# pool. It has already been deleted from this folder, but if it ever gets
# copied back in it must never enter this repo or this site.
Caledon Storefront.png

# The business card is not a website image and there is no slot for it.
Leamington Spray Foam Business Card.png

# Orphaned build artifact. build.py exports the social share graphic at 1200px
# as both webp and jpg, renames the jpg to og-image.jpg, then deletes the webp
# because og:image has to be a jpg. On this mounted drive that delete fails
# with "Operation not permitted", so the file survives every build. Nothing
# references it - og:image points at og-image.jpg - so it is ignored rather
# than committed. Deleting it by hand in File Explorer also works.
site/images/og-image-1200.webp
